{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <string>\n#include <regex>\n\nint main() {\n    std::string x;\n    std::cin >> x;\n    std::string y;\n    y.reserve(x.size());\n    y += x[0];\n    if (x.empty()) {\n        std::cout << y;\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    std::regex re(\"at(?=.)|dot(?=.)\");\n    std::size_t last = 1;\n    bool at_done = false;\n\n    auto begin = std::sregex_iterator(x.begin(), x.end(), re);\n    auto end = std::sregex_iterator();\n    for (auto it = begin; it != end; ++it) {\n        std::smatch m = *it;\n        std::size_t pos = static_cast<std::size_t>(m.position());\n        if (pos < last) continue;\n        std::string tok = m.str();\n\n        if (tok == \"at\" && !at_done) {\n            y.append(x, last, pos - last);\n            y.push_back('@');\n            last = pos + 2;\n            at_done = true;\n        } else if (tok == \"dot\") {\n            y.append(x, last, pos - last);\n            y.push_back('.');\n            last = pos + 3;\n        } else {\n            y.append(x, last, pos - last);\n            y += tok;\n            last = pos + 2;\n        }\n    }\n    y.append(x, last, std::string::npos);\n\n    std::cout << y;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\nimport java.util.regex.Matcher;\nimport java.util.regex.Pattern;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        String x = scanner.nextLine();\n        scanner.close();\n\n        // Handle empty input (original C++ code has undefined behavior for empty string)\n        if (x.isEmpty()) {\n            System.out.println();\n            return;\n        }\n\n        StringBuilder y = new StringBuilder();\n        y.append(x.charAt(0));\n\n        Pattern pattern = Pattern.compile(\"at(?=.)|dot(?=.)\");\n        Matcher matcher = pattern.matcher(x);\n        int last = 1;\n        boolean atDone = false;\n\n        while (matcher.find()) {\n            int pos = matcher.start();\n            if (pos < last) continue;\n            String tok = matcher.group();\n\n            if (tok.equals(\"at\") && !atDone) {\n                y.append(x, last, pos);\n                y.append('@');\n                last = pos + 2;\n                atDone = true;\n            } else if (tok.equals(\"dot\")) {\n                y.append(x, last, pos);\n                y.append('.');\n                last = pos + 3;\n            } else {\n                // This branch handles \"at\" when atDone is true (keep original)\n                y.append(x, last, pos);\n                y.append(tok);\n                last = pos + tok.length();\n            }\n        }\n        y.append(x, last, x.length());\n\n        System.out.println(y.toString());\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.004841984249651432, -3.0517112463712692e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -4.434487345861271e-05, -0.00022158552019391